Subject: util/disk_cache: add a Windows multi-file backend

Upstream Mesa (main at 66e82ef1, 2026-11-25, and 26.2.2) refuses
-Dshader-cache=enabled on Windows and leaves disk_cache_os.c as
"TODO: implement disk cache support on windows". This adds that backend.

- The entry format helpers (parse_and_validate_cache_item,
  create_cache_item_header_and_blob) and the Fossilize/database wrappers are
  shared; only file system calls differ.
- The Windows backend keeps the POSIX multi-file layout and entry format:
  <dir>/mesa_shader_cache/<2 hex>/<62 hex>, written to a .tmp file and
  renamed into place, plus the shared "index" file (size and key index).
  An exclusive share mode on the .tmp file stands in for flock(); the
  rename never replaces an existing entry, so the size accounting stays
  right.
- It uses only Win32 calls that AppContainer (UWP) binaries may make:
  CreateFile2, CreateDirectoryW, GetFileAttributesExW, MoveFileExW,
  DeleteFileW, FindFirstFileExW, and CreateFileMappingFromApp and
  MapViewOfFileFromApp under WINAPI_FAMILY_APP.
- Paths are UTF-8 internally and reach the wide file APIs with backslash
  separators in extended-length form (\\?\X:\...). A packaged app's
  LocalState path plus the cache's ~90 characters takes a temporary entry
  past MAX_PATH, where the C runtime's narrow file calls fail; the extended
  form has no such limit. Missing parent directories are created from the
  deepest existing one down, so the folders above an app's own storage are
  never touched.
- The directory must be named by MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR: a packaged process
  has no per-user default location, so without it the cache is disabled.
  The variable is read in its wide form. MESA_SHADER_CACHE_MAX_SIZE and
  MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE work as upstream.
- disk_cache_print_diagnostics() writes key=value lines for a driver's
  statistics file: whether the cache is usable, the step at which its
  directory setup stopped, its directory and size limit, and the entries
  queued. The Windows backend adds the entries written and read, the write
  and read failures, and the first failed file operation with its path and
  Win32 error. A storage failure is otherwise visible only as misses.
- disk_cache_wait_for_idle() does nothing for a cache without a queue
  (one whose directory could not be set up).
- On Windows the meson 'shader-cache' option stays off for 'auto' and is
  built with -Dshader-cache=enabled.
- Enabling the cache also builds shaderapi.c's shader-replacement code on
  Windows for the first time. Its empty replacement table was a zero-length
  array, which MSVC rejects (C2466); it now holds one entry that never
  matches.

